      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The curtain is down, and Toronto is playing out the string with the blunt honesty of a club that knows the calendar has beaten it. <strong>The Blue Jays dropped Saturday's finale-in-waiting 5-1 to the Reds</strong>, falling to 78-83 and fifth in the AL East, and now the only question left on Sunday is whether Max Scherzer's start will be his Toronto goodbye or merely a pause before an offseason decision. Trey Yesavage's brief cameo was the other telling note - a rookie getting over the finish line after a year of interruptions, the kind of look a lost season still owes itself. There's no playoff theater here, only cleanup work and a hard winter ahead. <strong>Watch Scherzer in the finale, then watch the front office sort out pitching depth and the young arms that deserve a longer look.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
