        "body": "The summer's big swing has already changed the tenor of camp - Toronto is no longer tiptoeing around expectations, with Kawhi Leonard in the fold and Bobby Webster raising the bar instead of lowering it. That matters because the Raptors enter camp with no wiggle room and no excuse, and the first test is sorting who fits beside Leonard, RJ Barrett and Jakob Poeltl as the rotation hardens. <strong>The real headline is who's in and who's out as camp opens</strong> - the lineup math, the health ledger, the rookies trying to crash the party. There's a preseason tune-up Saturday against Miami, then the proper accounting begins Oct. 21 against Chicago. <strong>What happens over the next two weeks will tell you whether this is a deep team or just an expensive one.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
