      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The early-season punchline has turned grim: Washington already sits at 0-2, fourth in the NFC East, and now has to answer the old question of survival without its young quarterback. <strong>Jayden Daniels is out for Week 3 with a left elbow injury, and Marcus Mariota takes the reins again</strong> - the kind of handoff that tells you how quickly a promising autumn can start leaning on duct tape. The Commanders were beaten 37-20 by Dallas last Sunday, and the two-loss skid has left them 2 games back before September is even done. Daniels' injury is the story, the stomach punch, the whole afternoon in one grim snapshot. Washington doesn't need a pep talk; it needs a clean pocket, a steady veteran, and a little dignity. <strong>Against Seattle today, the Commanders have to show they can keep the season from slipping into free fall</strong>.",
